{
  "id": "dev-dispatch-c",
  "name": "Version C: decompose + break big tasks into subtasks",
  "description": "When a spec card completes, route it to the right profile: bugs to debugger, research to scout, ops to ops, architecture to architect, everything else to tech-lead. Replaces the old cron-based dispatch.",
  "trigger": {
    "source": "card_completed",
    "condition": {
      "assignee": "product-owner",
      "status": "done",
      "title_prefix_any": [
        "[spec]",
        "[ticket-"
      ]
    }
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "entry",
      "profile": "product-owner",
      "type": "command",
      "command": "echo '{\"status\": \"routing\"}'",
      "body_template": "noop — routing junction"
    },
    {
      "id": "route-bug",
      "profile": "debugger",
      "body_template": "## Bug to investigate\n\nSpec: ${trigger.card_id}\nTitle: ${trigger.title}\n\nInvestigate the root cause. Run your debug-loop (reproduce → fix → converge).\n\nComplete this card with metadata:\n```\n{verdict: \"fixed\"|\"escalated-design\"|\"blocked-hitl\", fix_commit: \"<sha>\", branch_name: \"<branch>\", regression_test: \"<path>\", root_cause_summary: \"<one-line>\", changed_files: [\"...\"]}\n```",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "verdict"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "verdict": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "fixed",
                "escalated-design",
                "blocked-hitl"
              ]
            },
            "fix_commit": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "branch_name": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "regression_test": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "root_cause_summary": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "changed_files": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "route-scout",
      "profile": "scout",
      "body_template": "## Research task\n\nSpec: ${trigger.card_id}\nTitle: ${trigger.title}\n\nInvestigate this question against high-trust primary sources. Record your findings.\n\nComplete this card with metadata {verdict: \"done\", summary: \"<one-line>\"} when done.",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "verdict"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "verdict": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "done"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "route-ops",
      "profile": "ops",
      "body_template": "## Ops task\n\nSpec: ${trigger.card_id}\nTitle: ${trigger.title}\n\nExecute this operational task.\n\nComplete this card with metadata {verdict: \"done\"} when done."
    },
    {
      "id": "route-architect",
      "profile": "architect",
      "body_template": "## Architecture decision needed\n\nSpec: ${trigger.card_id}\nTitle: ${trigger.title}\n\nAnswer in gate posture: weigh alternatives before deciding. Record the decision as an ADR.\n\nComplete this card with metadata {verdict: \"decided\", adr: \"ADR-NNN\"} when done.",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "verdict"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "verdict": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "decided",
                "needs-more-info"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "route-tech-lead",
      "profile": "product-owner",
      "skill": "to-tickets",
      "body_template": "## Decompose + subtask nesting\n\n**Spec card:** ${trigger.card_id}\n**Title:** ${trigger.title}\n\nYou are the product-owner. DO NOT implement. Your job has TWO phases.\n\n### Phase 1: Initial decomposition\n\nRead the spec. Load your `to-tickets` skill. Decompose into atomic tasks. Create [ticket-NN] cards assigned to tech-lead with dependencies via kanban_create.\n\n### Phase 2: Granularity review + subtask nesting (CRITICAL)\n\nAfter creating all ticket cards, review EACH one. For each ticket, check:\n- Can a junior dev complete it in one sitting?\n- Does it have clear, testable acceptance criteria?\n- Can it be verified independently?\n- Is it a single concern (not two tasks disguised as one)?\n\nIf a ticket is TOO BIG (fails any check), do NOT delete it. Instead, create subtask cards as CHILDREN of the oversized ticket:\n- `title`: \"[subtask-NN-MM] <subtask title>\"\n- `assignee`: \"tech-lead\"\n- `body`: the subtask's specific acceptance criteria\n- `parents`: [the oversized ticket's card id]\n\nThis preserves the original ticket as a parent container while breaking the work into smaller pieces underneath. The parent ticket stays in todo until all its subtasks complete.\n\n### Completion metadata\n\nAfter ALL tickets (and subtasks) are created, complete with:\n```\n{decomposed: true, ticket_count: N, ticket_ids: [\"<id1>\", ...], subtask_count: N, subtask_parents: [\"<id>\", ...]}\n```",
      "title_template": "[decompose-c] ${trigger.title}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "decomposed",
            "ticket_count",
            "ticket_ids"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "decomposed": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "ticket_count": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "ticket_ids": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "subtask_count": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "subtask_parents": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "route-tickets",
      "profile": "product-owner",
      "skill": "",
      "body_template": "## Parse pre-made tickets — create cards with dependencies\n\n**Source card:** ${trigger.card_id}\n**Title:** ${trigger.title}\n\nYou are the product-owner. DO NOT decompose. DO NOT plan. DO NOT implement. Your ONLY job is to parse the ticket definitions from the source card body and create one kanban card per ticket with correct dependencies.\n\n### Phase 1: Parse\n\nRead the source card body. It contains pre-made ticket definitions in this format:\n\n```\n## Ticket NN — <title>\n**Blocked by:** NN, NN (or \"none\")\n**Body:** <what to build>\n```\n\nParse each ticket block. Extract: number, title, blocked-by list, body text.\n\n### Phase 2: Create cards (CRITICAL)\n\nFor EACH ticket, create a card via `kanban_create`:\n- `title`: \"[ticket-NN] <ticket title>\"\n- `assignee`: \"tech-lead\"\n- `body`: the ticket's body text (what to build)\n- `parents`: list of ticket card ids for each \"Blocked by\" entry\n\nCREATE IN DEPENDENCY ORDER: Layer 0 (no blockers) first, then Layer 1, etc. This ensures parent card ids exist before children reference them in `parents`.\n\nEach ticket fires tech-lead-execute independently when tech-lead completes it.\n\nDO NOT call kanban_chains. DO NOT call loop_engine. DO NOT decompose. DO NOT implement.\n\n### Completion metadata\n\nAfter creating ALL ticket cards, complete this card with:\n```\n{decomposed: true, ticket_count: N, ticket_ids: [\"<id1>\", \"<id2>\", ...]}\n```",
      "title_template": "[dispatch] ${trigger.title}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "decomposed",
            "ticket_count",
            "ticket_ids"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "decomposed": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "ticket_count": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "ticket_ids": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "from": "entry",
      "to": "route-bug",
      "condition": "${trigger.type} == 'bug'"
    },
    {
      "from": "entry",
      "to": "route-scout",
      "condition": "${trigger.type} == 'research'"
    },
    {
      "from": "entry",
      "to": "route-ops",
      "condition": "${trigger.type} == 'ops'"
    },
    {
      "from": "entry",
      "to": "route-architect",
      "condition": "${trigger.type} == 'architecture'"
    },
    {
      "from": "entry",
      "to": "route-tickets",
      "condition": "${trigger.type} == 'tickets'"
    },
    {
      "from": "entry",
      "to": "route-tech-lead",
      "condition": "${trigger.type} != 'bug' AND ${trigger.type} != 'research' AND ${trigger.type} != 'ops' AND ${trigger.type} != 'architecture' AND ${trigger.type} != 'tickets'"
    }
  ]
}